 <li><strong>Fleet</strong>: worn, past its lifespan, idle in a depot.</li>
 <li><strong>Economy</strong>: lines that lost money over the last 12 months (in at least 3 of the 4 quarters), and lines whose average utilisation over about a year is very low. Bigger losses and emptier lines get a higher severity.</li>
 <li><strong>Fleet window</strong>: the ↑ Upg button on an Old or Worn vehicle's row opens a Fleet window for its line: vehicles (how many are past their lifespan or worn), capacity, current load with a utilisation bar, frequency, passengers and cargo transported per year and the average age against the lifespan, next to the last 12 months' income, running costs, maintenance and balance. Fleet by model lists each model with its count, the oldest vehicle's age and how many are past their lifespan.</li>
-<li><strong>Upgrade</strong>: "Upgrade old vehicles", "Upgrade this vehicle", "Upgrade whole fleet" and the "Upgrade N…" button on each model open the game's own Replace Vehicles window with those vehicles, where you pick the new model and confirm the price. Replaced vehicles leave the radar at once. "Show line" opens the line's window.</li>
+<li><strong>Upgrade</strong>: "Upgrade old vehicles", "Upgrade this vehicle", "Upgrade whole fleet" and, on a line with several models, the "Upgrade N…" button on each model open the game's own Replace Vehicles window with those vehicles, where you pick the new model and confirm the price. Replaced vehicles leave the radar at once. "Show line" opens the line's window.</li>
 <li><strong>Badge</strong>: a small badge or a compact one-row panel in the top-left button ridge shows the number of problems, coloured by the worst severity.</li>
 <li><strong>Tabs</strong> for All, Vehicles, Lines, Stations, Fleet and Economy, each with its count, plus Snoozed and Settings. Click a row to move the camera there and open the vehicle, line or station window.</li>
 <li><strong>Notifications</strong>: each alert type can be set to Off, List (shown in the radar only) or Notify (also a game notification when the problem first appears). Notifications are rate-limited and can be paused.</li>
